# BNOW.NET — environment-variable EXAMPLES (documentation only).
#
# Every line is commented on purpose: this file must never carry an active
# assignment or a secret. Copy the lines you need into your own .env.local
# (gitignored) or the Vercel environment. The authoritative credentials table
# lives in AGENTS.md; spend-cap semantics are standing ruling 4.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud-model routing (src/lib/llm/model-config.ts) — resolved at CALL time.
# Precedence per analysis workload: <WORKLOAD>_MODEL → OPENAI_MODEL → gpt-4o-mini.
# Blank/whitespace values are treated as absent. Dispatch FAILS CLOSED unless
# the resolved model has BOTH an exact price in src/lib/llm/pricing.ts
# PRICES_PER_MTOK and a quality-registry approval for the exact (workload,
# model, effort) in src/lib/llm/analysis-registry.ts — pricing alone is not
# quality approval. Reasoning efforts accept minimal|low|medium|high, apply
# only to reasoning models (gpt-5 family / o-series), and FAIL CLOSED when
# invalid or set on a non-reasoning model.
#
# MAP IS ADDITIONALLY HARD-LOCKED to its baseline (gpt-4o-mini, no effort):
# changing MAP_MODEL or MAP_REASONING_EFFORT changes mapExtractorVersion() but
# does NOT remap historical documents by itself (the hourly worker selects
# processed=false docs only), so every consumer of current-version claims
# would starve until the corpus is explicitly remapped. The version-aware
# remap operator exists (scripts/map-remap.ts — dry-run-first, resumable,
# lease-safe; OPEN-TASKS #33), but the lock stays: any non-baseline map
# configuration fails closed with "MAP ACTIVATION BLOCKED" — no env override
# exists; explicit operator activation authorization (with a costed remap of
# the corpus) relaxes it. REDUCE_MODEL changes are independent and never trip it.
# Inspect the resolved matrix without any provider call:
#   npx tsx scripts/model-routing-inspect.ts
#
# NONE of these are set anywhere today (2026-08-17). Activating any of them is
# gated on: verified pricing in pricing.ts, request-compatibility checks, a
# representative paid evaluation, spend-cap review, and operator authorization
# (docs/reviews/CLOUD-MODEL-ROUTING-SEAMS-2026-08-17.md § activation checklist).
#
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # global fallback for every analysis workload
# MAP_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                 # map stage (per-doc claim extraction)
# MAP_REASONING_EFFORT=low              # reasoning models only
# REDUCE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # mapreduce digest synthesis votes
# REDUCE_REASONING_EFFORT=medium        # reasoning models only
# DIGEST_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # legacy digest extraction
# DIGEST_REASONING_EFFORT=low           # reasoning models only
# VALIDATION_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini          # ISW scoreboard LLM matcher
# VALIDATION_REASONING_EFFORT=low       # reasoning models only
# ENTITY_AUDIT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini        # propose-only entity audit
# ENTITY_AUDIT_REASONING_EFFORT=low     # reasoning models only
#
# Ask pipeline models are NOT routed by model-config (scorecard-gated —
# src/lib/ask/registry.ts):
# ASK_ANSWER_MODEL=gpt-5
# ASK_RERANK_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map-stage concurrency lease (src/lib/analysis/map-lease.ts, provider_state
# key 'map_lease'): serializes the hourly cron, the backfill driver, and the
# remap operator. TTL seconds; clamped to [30, 600] so it can neither thrash
# nor outlive the map route's 800s maxDuration. Default 120.
# MAP_LEASE_TTL_SEC=120
